values ('b4c5d6e7-8f9a-4b81-8c01-1e2f3a4b5c11', 'special-education-inclusive-practices', 'Special Education / Inclusive Practices', 'This course prepares elementary educators to create accessible, ambitious, inclusive learning environments and fulfill their responsibilities to students with disabilities. Students integrate legal foundations, disability perspectives, evaluation and IEP processes, UDL, specially designed instruction, MTSS, behavior support, assistive technology, collaboration, equity, transition, safety, and field-based practice. Inclusion is defined by belonging, participation, learning, agency, and progress—not location alone.');

