  'Special Education / Inclusive Practices',
  'Special Education / Inclusive Practices',
  'This course prepares elementary educators to create accessible, ambitious, inclusive learning environments and fulfill their responsibilities to students with disabilities. Students integrate legal foundations, disability perspectives, evaluation and IEP processes, UDL, specially designed instruction, MTSS, behavior support, assistive technology, collaboration, equity, transition, safety, and field-based practice. Inclusion is defined by belonging, participation, learning, agency, and progress—not location alone.',
  $seipjson${"slug": "special-education-inclusive-practices", "title": "Special Education / Inclusive Practices", "description": "This course prepares elementary educators to create accessible, ambitious, inclusive learning environments and fulfill their responsibilities to students with disabilities. Students integrate legal foundations, disability perspectives, evaluation and IEP processes, UDL, specially designed instruction, MTSS, behavior support, assistive technology, collaboration, equity, transition, safety, and field-based practice. Inclusion is defined by belonging, participation, learning, agency, and progress—not location alone.", "topics": [{"id": "32e0925b-c193-45b5-83ad-4b2e4cef8fd1", "type": "topic", "title": "1. Disability, Inclusion, and the History of Special Education", "description": "Understand how disability models, activism, segregation, and rights movements shape present-day schools and teacher responsibilities.", "children": [{"id": "c9794e3f-e272-4915-8525-2ce85f76404e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical development", "children": [{"id": "4d841ba5-4e2f-4fae-a70c-0b003a280199", "type": "concept", "title": "Compulsory schooling and exclusion"}, {"id": "37b4b1f9-99b5-466f-b5b1-2f5849ebe3d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Parent/self-advocacy and disability-rights movements"}, {"id": "81fe2cb1-49ef-4d55-bd32-88cc966f7bd7", "type": "concept", "title": "From separate services toward inclusive systems"}], "description": "Students trace exclusion, institutionalization, litigation, and inclusion."}, {"id": "9b106379-ca09-4bea-9971-8f21f433baea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Models of disability", "children": [{"id": "6f559eac-8a9f-4a1b-8ce5-d13e6387f018", "type": "concept", "title": "Medical, deficit, social, human-rights, and interactional models"}, {"id": "201eb476-9bc9-4c8c-937a-8fdd1b065855", "type": "concept", "title": "Neurodiversity and disability culture"}, {"id": "07bcb703-cc54-4daa-9c27-0728d8ca6f80", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths, needs, identity, and context"}], "description": "The point is distinguishing impairment from socially created barriers."}, {"id": "1fc7f5ac-fd46-459a-9e9d-c6fbec270168", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ableism and belonging", "children": [{"id": "660144d3-4aca-4745-bfaa-1d1656c66c55", "type": "concept", "title": "Language, stigma, inspiration/pity narratives, and microaggressions"}, {"id": "78311c97-b829-40fa-a666-0e73d060a714", "type": "concept", "title": "Presumed competence and dignity of risk"}, {"id": "3852fde1-c6bb-4d8a-91fc-af2c89621dd5", "type": "concept", "title": "Membership, peer relationships, and classroom community"}], "description": "Students identify low expectations and exclusionary routines."}]}, {"id": "a4865cdf-a885-4779-9341-deac35d2d068", "type": "topic", "title": "2. IDEA, Section 504, ADA, and Educational Rights", "description": "Apply core legal principles while recognizing that state rules and district procedures require current verification.", "children": [{"id": "c25518f0-44a6-4ca7-9e70-5701d06ec12a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IDEA framework", "children": [{"id": "596bef34-27a9-4a56-bc19-54a7a94bdb9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Child Find and zero reject"}, {"id": "ecb3d0a6-c355-48d3-a1c1-f301e0b3ad2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Free appropriate public education and meaningful progress"}, {"id": "b79cb3a0-749b-46e3-8d3b-b853d935310b", "type": "concept", "title": "Least restrictive environment and continuum of placements"}], "description": "Students understand FAPE, LRE, evaluation, IEP, safeguards, and related services."}, {"id": "49d788a7-4768-4331-b018-dcf9811a4231", "type": "subtopic", "title": "504 and ADA", "children": [{"id": "78d795c7-0f5f-47f9-bbae-2fe51176b518", "type": "concept", "title": "Disability definition and reasonable accommodation"}, {"id": "b45eaa0e-5e3f-4da1-bc77-e91fb61111da", "type": "concept", "title": "Program, facility, communication, and digital access"}, {"id": "555887be-618d-424d-89d3-851733dad865", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparison of IEP and 504 protections"}], "description": "The goal is access and nondiscrimination beyond IDEA eligibility."}, {"id": "89ec7e11-0d93-4470-a03c-d077e4b16ed5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Procedural rights and responsibility", "children": [{"id": "931597d3-527e-4c29-b315-1fa5ac4c644e", "type": "concept", "title": "Notice, consent, records, participation, dispute resolution, and confidentiality"}, {"id": "8bc321d8-fc3e-4ab1-87bd-39b78140af88", "type": "concept", "title": "Teacher access to and responsibility for IEP provisions"}, {"id": "7afc67f0-f0c1-459a-b9c8-2c5ebfbe6bf1", "type": "concept", "title": "State/district policy, documentation, and consultation"}], "description": "Students know their role in timely, accurate implementation."}]}, {"id": "844ada98-33ab-4913-91b1-7e215227afa7", "type": "topic", "title": "3. Disability Categories, Individual Variability, and Strengths", "description": "Use category knowledge as a starting point—not a prediction of any learner’s abilities or needs.", "children": [{"id": "52c94698-c400-47e1-b7f5-6a95f0632fc8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IDEA categories", "children": [{"id": "a132832c-653e-437a-9489-2afb351a9a2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Learning disability, speech/language, autism, intellectual disability, emotional disability"}, {"id": "945a0f83-3eb3-4527-a02f-3b4cdd5894f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Other health impairment, orthopedic, sensory, brain injury, multiple disabilities"}, {"id": "05fb0dec-2f2d-4ded-bd5d-666e9ae6c1fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Deaf-blindness and developmental delay"}], "description": "Students learn broad characteristics and educational implications."}, {"id": "b749e52f-2d78-438e-aebf-470621c181e6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Within-group variability", "children": [{"id": "281eeac0-28b5-445c-87c4-f511b3331f76", "type": "concept", "title": "Comorbidity and multiple identities"}, {"id": "28c51701-74c4-4540-8bc8-56de339334f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Severity, context, development, culture, and opportunity"}, {"id": "f1e142cf-34f1-416c-a697-d9a8a9a5072e", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths, interests, preferences, and communication"}], "description": "The point is individualized assessment and instruction."}, {"id": "25e6dc19-ece9-4756-8143-8b7a6c0f911d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Avoiding diagnostic overshadowing", "children": [{"id": "48fd162f-6636-4911-b0c3-0be6ac12f70e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural/linguistic difference versus disability"}, {"id": "10419c12-4394-4b38-a419-c9733a7c6f6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias in referral and identification"}, {"id": "e2373fc8-01c4-456e-b62a-44a76bdf3d1f", "type": "concept", "title": "High expectations and access to grade-level content"}], "description": "Students distinguish disability-related need from instruction, language, trauma, health, and environment."}]}, {"id": "ef3239cc-8e48-482b-84e5-6a34bcf5b1b7", "type": "topic", "title": "4. Child Find, Referral, Evaluation, and Eligibility", "description": "Recognize possible disability, document high-quality instruction/support, and participate in comprehensive, nondiscriminatory evaluation.", "children": [{"id": "6fb1614b-70f3-4545-ac85-dad617b1e826", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pre-referral and Child Find", "children": [{"id": "c7e7617f-e06a-4b89-b701-4f0437ddf505", "type": "concept", "title": "Concern identification and family communication"}, {"id": "001d9959-3d75-4b5f-b847-19ac199d55f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Instructional history and intervention data"}, {"id": "794890b5-4a1c-499e-9a6d-8b72b33d10ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Vision, hearing, attendance, language, mobility, and health context"}], "description": "Students understand that MTSS cannot be used to delay a warranted evaluation."}, {"id": "72942128-ea86-4bfe-b47d-efb8f2ee9ffa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evaluation principles", "children": [{"id": "fa2e5421-8048-4ca4-b957-51477db1dc5f", "type": "concept", "title": "Academic, functional, developmental, behavioral, communication, and adaptive information"}, {"id": "78e910e7-7b33-4171-9500-12c06a1c96c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Validity, language, accessibility, bias, and testing accommodations"}, {"id": "6262e5d6-dd8b-4506-9049-facb86f25f04", "type": "concept", "title": "No single measure as sole criterion"}], "description": "The goal is multiple tools and sources tied to educational need."}, {"id": "27c5ffab-24b2-4d10-a572-4db7ed246f93", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Eligibility and planning", "children": [{"id": "b5b7af04-9afb-45be-a801-eef76784f9e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Multidisciplinary decision making"}, {"id": "b4411982-1d84-4c76-9e36-0af8044fc4b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Adverse educational impact and need for specially designed instruction"}, {"id": "8825e125-28f6-47c7-bc5f-513c783c9882", "type": "concept", "title": "Reevaluation and independent educational evaluation concepts"}], "description": "Students distinguish diagnosis from IDEA eligibility and service need."}]}, {"id": "f87a5a82-69de-4ae1-8133-650eeba2aae5", "type": "topic", "title": "5. IEP Development, Implementation, and Progress", "description": "Translate evaluation and student/family priorities into a coherent, measurable educational program.", "children": [{"id": "62e9d665-661d-4102-bdd9-56ccf221c6c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Present levels and needs", "children": [{"id": "3bcd8a09-4c72-446f-af6a-834d6a8a7bd0", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths, family/student concerns, evaluation data, and access to curriculum"}, {"id": "eefd3b2b-2529-4022-9490-ef241f61ff01", "type": "concept", "title": "Disability impact and priority needs"}, {"id": "8eef4e3a-8728-442c-baff-08a3c890d827", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline data and conditions"}], "description": "Students write specific descriptions of current academic and functional performance."}, {"id": "fd192c15-8b4b-4ef1-8fae-e2f16f909567", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Goals and services", "children": [{"id": "b60df36b-d1f0-46ab-bc35-c9a7090e8980", "type": "concept", "title": "Annual goals with behavior, condition, criterion, and timeframe"}, {"id": "6842e7e7-cc99-4c56-9474-8d38485ef773", "type": "concept", "title": "Specially designed instruction, related services, supplementary aids, and program modifications"}, {"id": "7d3f996a-b494-4af1-9023-098687091188", "type": "concept", "title": "Frequency, duration, location, personnel, and assistive technology"}], "description": "The point is measurable progress and aligned support."}, {"id": "e68a7028-891f-4858-ae83-4433885f146c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Implementation and monitoring", "children": [{"id": "caad5520-8a12-4754-8a08-8fb363619f6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Teacher responsibilities and communication"}, {"id": "77c380f3-3100-4511-b69f-be41b54bfc27", "type": "concept", "title": "Data collection, progress reports, and team review"}, {"id": "1ed744b8-349d-4a2d-a863-072bd5952742", "type": "concept", "title": "Amendment, annual review, and response when progress is insufficient"}], "description": "Students ensure the written plan becomes daily practice."}]}, {"id": "95f71876-0e38-4e27-9b56-bc78cad85d89", "type": "topic", "title": "6. Least Restrictive Environment and Inclusive Placement", "description": "Design supports that enable meaningful membership, participation, learning, and progress in general education.", "children": [{"id": "6186e2fc-7c1a-4988-9265-ce9543cde70c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "LRE decision making", "children": [{"id": "37611632-0a86-4b16-bf7d-3b5806ff8d3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Education with nondisabled peers to maximum appropriate extent"}, {"id": "896c2c4b-901c-4cb3-bb98-d6b11e3bc56b", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplementary aids/services before removal"}, {"id": "686ec1dc-2387-425d-8d58-57649f07f987", "type": "concept", "title": "Academic and nonacademic settings"}], "description": "Students understand individualized placement after goals/services are defined."}, {"id": "7c28918c-40fa-45a5-9f14-6d5f9617e575", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Meaningful inclusion", "children": [{"id": "4e3d2c33-1315-4786-b481-372bf9a90cdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Grade-level standards and adapted access"}, {"id": "f697e27e-ef5c-458f-8628-a8c8a13ce2c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer relationships, classroom roles, and extracurriculars"}, {"id": "d380f27f-2b77-4671-a875-0a86a8994669", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding one-to-one adult dependence and social isolation"}], "description": "The goal is participation with belonging and learning—not physical presence alone."}, {"id": "5698f811-efc1-4baa-92f0-c3d5357578a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive school systems", "children": [{"id": "f9313387-23e7-4f7c-9b1c-20f5056db619", "type": "concept", "title": "Collaborative planning time"}, {"id": "f192ce35-39ce-4b08-a6bb-5b5b1383d040", "type": "concept", "title": "Flexible grouping and service delivery"}, {"id": "5e500f88-0cb2-4ab5-889a-1a282335b002", "type": "concept", "title": "Schoolwide culture, accessibility, and accountability"}], "description": "Students examine scheduling, staffing, leadership, and resources."}]}, {"id": "817229ab-23d3-41cf-a7bd-372491712a35", "type": "topic", "title": "7. Universal Design for Learning and Accessible Environments", "description": "Proactively reduce barriers and expand learner agency through flexible goals, materials, methods, and participation.", "children": [{"id": "c479d502-bd78-4103-8a39-f0b6a2e83999", "type": "subtopic", "title": "UDL design process", "children": [{"id": "fb7ea57c-477d-4210-9941-535f43b7c5fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple means of engagement"}, {"id": "9dfe152b-8a62-4aa3-b5a3-50859925a311", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple means of representation"}, {"id": "11b73477-eab1-40ed-ac44-f22a76f411c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple means of action and expression"}], "description": "Students use CAST Guidelines 3.0 as a planning lens rather than a checklist."}, {"id": "82238f90-1924-483f-b936-46d90ff685c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessible materials and technology", "children": [{"id": "79425e82-aef6-4b0b-9abf-71a030d281f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Readable layouts, captions, alt text, audio, tactile and translated formats"}, {"id": "7ec7a75c-7e90-40f7-b921-7da664e9091b", "type": "concept", "title": "Keyboard/switch access and accessible documents/platforms"}, {"id": "924ecb64-e6d2-4b9a-adbf-4bcba76665e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible educational materials and procurement"}], "description": "The point is access at the same time as peers."}, {"id": "59c2ced5-30a0-41dc-9e8b-2597a3a6b8f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Learner agency", "children": [{"id": "8aee9b7c-0ca0-411b-b1ad-5237529db9c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Choice without lowering essential goals"}, {"id": "65561f0d-be34-4de3-930b-a08d6cf41a7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Goal setting, strategy, self-monitoring, and reflection"}, {"id": "0ec5fbcf-af9d-4271-820f-b1f14f7ad711", "type": "concept", "title": "Identity, joy, relevance, challenge, and belonging"}], "description": "Students cultivate purposeful, resourceful, strategic learning."}]}, {"id": "5a135d10-8cbb-464a-b790-1f9630473c39", "type": "topic", "title": "8. Specially Designed Instruction, Differentiation, and Scaffolding", "description": "Adapt content, methodology, or delivery to address disability-related needs while preserving ambitious learning goals.", "children": [{"id": "14648763-4199-4759-b6e1-72083a1f975e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Instructional design", "children": [{"id": "15f92bbf-bfbc-43f3-9d58-e1a56bc738e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Clear goals and success criteria"}, {"id": "fa4dcd01-5c88-41f9-9cd6-a06451f6c9fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Modeling, guided practice, feedback, and cumulative review"}, {"id": "8892afeb-0353-4966-8c89-93c4ede9c9e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Task analysis and systematic instruction"}], "description": "Students identify the barrier and teach the missing knowledge/skill explicitly."}, {"id": "c17b6765-2578-4a0b-adcb-e659c39804d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Differentiation and scaffolds", "children": [{"id": "8ca517b7-5e73-41c5-866a-c0698e7095f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Content, process, product, environment, and time"}, {"id": "45254e07-7cde-4797-a211-40cf7c26b73c", "type": "concept", "title": "Visuals, organizers, prompts, worked examples, and peer supports"}, {"id": "b569f5d4-9cc2-4604-8489-77165b4fd117", "type": "concept", "title": "Prompt fading and independence"}], "description": "The goal is temporary or enduring support matched to need."}, {"id": "e3508c58-b6bc-47bf-adc1-97f1de85acc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accommodations versus modifications", "children": [{"id": "df830b00-ae7a-41d2-b604-655ded6b5598", "type": "concept", "title": "Presentation, response, setting, timing/scheduling"}, {"id": "8de024c6-2dca-4311-928f-91151cba9f19", "type": "concept", "title": "Assignment/curriculum modifications and grading implications"}, {"id": "fe863bc5-aca7-43e7-bf99-68df04c294ec", "type": "concept", "title": "IEP alignment and documentation"}], "description": "Students distinguish access changes from changes to learning expectations."}]}, {"id": "3f22f53b-f805-4ba4-9de8-433b245eaea8", "type": "topic", "title": "9. Inclusive Literacy Instruction", "description": "Provide evidence-based reading and writing instruction with intensified, accessible support.", "children": [{"id": "9f9a7c54-88ce-4729-a43e-3f56eedcae90", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Foundational reading", "children": [{"id": "d2a0ee0d-420b-4682-8c19-f9066ddad20d", "type": "concept", "title": "Phonological awareness, decoding, fluency, spelling, and morphology"}, {"id": "645ea520-2e92-4e51-9db6-a4ca6f4dbeac", "type": "concept", "title": "Systematic cumulative instruction and practice"}, {"id": "1ac846f7-5b1e-4912-8871-4d703bc874ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Dyslexia concepts and misconceptions"}], "description": "Students connect explicit instruction to individual data."}, {"id": "d56b69fe-b844-40d4-9ad6-5a7bfec00e05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Language and comprehension", "children": [{"id": "69ae09ce-1bc3-4ada-b33a-996fc27d9359", "type": "concept", "title": "Oral language and background knowledge"}, {"id": "391ac730-f694-4f59-af95-0aecab745145", "type": "concept", "title": "Text structure, questioning, summarizing, and inference"}, {"id": "c9212c5a-2cb2-4ad1-8d20-6fd89bb552db", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible text and read-aloud/text-to-speech decisions"}], "description": "The point is building knowledge, vocabulary, syntax, and strategic meaning."}, {"id": "c89550b0-9c8a-4049-b380-6f3c4f3479f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Writing", "children": [{"id": "1ff2adef-7cb3-43cc-a3f5-6b2838832493", "type": "concept", "title": "Handwriting/keyboard, spelling, sentence construction, and planning"}, {"id": "6ce1b60d-1ff2-4b77-9d42-a1bce11d443d", "type": "concept", "title": "Graphic organizers, models, feedback, and assistive tools"}, {"id": "96764e01-7e35-4217-aa49-69addd1b8004", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternative expression while teaching writing skills"}], "description": "Students support transcription and composition."}]}, {"id": "7ccb7c97-90a0-4021-8d62-dfb97faa5b56", "type": "topic", "title": "10. Inclusive Mathematics and Content-Area Instruction", "description": "Make mathematical reasoning, science, and social studies accessible through explicit teaching and multiple representations.", "children": [{"id": "95667ece-e8c5-4471-8478-960feb67a44e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mathematics", "children": [{"id": "92aa8259-56fc-4dcd-8e1c-600262055546", "type": "concept", "title": "Concrete–representational–abstract sequences"}, {"id": "dc3ce646-bc7c-4188-9c76-a203c14d7c01", "type": "concept", "title": "Number sense, computation, problem solving, and vocabulary"}, {"id": "a9febaf6-61ad-4419-8e0e-329fc5c46d61", "type": "concept", "title": "Worked examples, cumulative review, and error analysis"}], "description": "Students diagnose conceptual, procedural, language, and memory barriers."}, {"id": "2e51da2b-782e-4885-a575-61e52377e9c5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Science and social studies", "children": [{"id": "f334c921-8542-4d98-965e-6b689fa46b33", "type": "concept", "title": "Vocabulary, background knowledge, text features, and source analysis"}, {"id": "667e1ac1-e02f-46ec-ae05-335243cde40b", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible labs, maps, timelines, models, and simulations"}, {"id": "3d194560-98d5-44c6-81f4-07312630d9e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety and adaptive equipment"}], "description": "The goal is participation in inquiry and disciplinary thinking."}, {"id": "15051715-78da-4797-861d-010ba8657334", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Generalization and application", "children": [{"id": "ab724e60-c392-4a8f-837c-8b72012119cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple exemplars and varied practice"}, {"id": "aedef693-e3a3-4bdd-ba66-ee748e2c81c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Real-world problem solving"}, {"id": "b0932a57-2296-43ee-97de-0bc0f88589b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-monitoring and strategy transfer"}], "description": "Students connect learning across settings and tasks."}]}, {"id": "373c4752-7154-4dd2-8c2a-c245ac9ffea1", "type": "topic", "title": "11. MTSS, RTI, and Data-Based Individualization", "description": "Use a prevention-oriented continuum of academic, behavioral, and social-emotional supports while preserving legal evaluation rights.", "children": [{"id": "d1785f7c-a5c6-4e77-abfb-c251bf761ec3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tiered system", "children": [{"id": "32ffcfaa-cf79-4b69-bef1-45065d2eb5a5", "type": "concept", "title": "High-quality Tier 1"}, {"id": "9ffc9ee5-a977-42b2-a46b-77fb899149cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Targeted Tier 2"}, {"id": "9bab76d2-8c22-4039-9ac2-a3eed4cec0a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Intensive individualized Tier 3"}], "description": "Students distinguish intensity from placement."}, {"id": "43ecf1a5-cb1d-4877-8dba-1de10e88d43b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data-based decisions", "children": [{"id": "e816c30c-566f-4512-aedf-62a9c02f379d", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal screening and diagnostic assessment"}, {"id": "eb548c8a-808c-4b13-9175-b403bdf26f9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Progress monitoring and decision rules"}, {"id": "91c8603a-699a-4aa2-972a-1508bca8b351", "type": "concept", "title": "Fidelity, attendance, opportunity, and intervention dosage"}], "description": "The point is responsiveness, not waiting to fail."}, {"id": "30a8eeab-a855-4198-b4f0-392f3aef4e14", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intensification", "children": [{"id": "04620024-2b08-419f-b1b7-5ed245c39751", "type": "concept", "title": "Strength, dosage, alignment, comprehensiveness, and behavioral support"}, {"id": "dffd2d9a-ee9b-46ff-bd60-5af210019185", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypothesis-driven changes"}, {"id": "68216abc-c110-4864-b5f1-f52f8657ba99", "type": "concept", "title": "Coordination with special education evaluation and IEP"}], "description": "Students adapt support systematically."}]}, {"id": "993b6f0e-440a-41ce-88d6-fba2b628399b", "type": "topic", "title": "12. Inclusive Assessment and Progress Monitoring", "description": "Collect fair, instructionally useful evidence and allow students accessible ways to demonstrate learning.", "children": [{"id": "8661695c-eb20-445b-bb54-3d5d66d90658", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assessment purposes", "children": [{"id": "c9ef8f9d-8214-4bd4-b855-0d2e9345f173", "type": "concept", "title": "Question-to-measure alignment"}, {"id": "da4554d8-1c7e-49b2-a4e0-f0b0ce4c4053", "type": "concept", "title": "Curriculum-based measurement concepts"}, {"id": "ca0ce515-3e45-40dd-b955-8c56c21157ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance and portfolio evidence"}], "description": "Students distinguish screening, diagnostic, formative, summative, and progress monitoring."}, {"id": "e62b3162-f435-451a-8c68-8d3a57dc0d58", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessible assessment", "children": [{"id": "e1a40124-0fd6-423e-b6ff-a00ff375cb81", "type": "concept", "title": "IEP/504 accommodations"}, {"id": "a1d23122-4189-4276-a766-d37c206d875c", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal design and accessible formats"}, {"id": "0da0c9c0-5633-48ce-8dd9-7e4c08fb2b21", "type": "concept", "title": "Language, culture, disability, and test bias"}], "description": "The goal is measuring the intended construct."}, {"id": "8160bf21-fea5-4ee2-88c1-5848b13702b2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using results", "children": [{"id": "0ebfd34e-cfc7-409b-871c-cd4d2020466a", "type": "concept", "title": "Graphing level, trend, variability, and goal line"}, {"id": "d1d84914-0f23-4904-acd5-d2e46441c05f", "type": "concept", "title": "Error/pattern analysis"}, {"id": "e1e9f9df-f222-44ae-a348-3a4a1432c87e", "type": "concept", "title": "Student/family-friendly reporting and team decisions"}], "description": "Students translate data into instruction and communication."}]}, {"id": "b27a5603-8704-492e-9a49-ce3d3288b7fe", "type": "topic", "title": "13. Positive Behavior Support, FBA, and BIP", "description": "Understand behavior as communication and design proactive, instructional, function-based support.", "children": [{"id": "85f155ae-abb9-41ab-894e-a911169fb07c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prevention and classroom systems", "children": [{"id": "881e3027-78f7-4d12-a1f0-8d049cb2dc5d", "type": "concept", "title": "Relationships, routines, expectations, active supervision, and opportunities to respond"}, {"id": "49bfd9a6-f10f-438c-9ce1-0e5d2b6cd45d", "type": "concept", "title": "Choice, engagement, precorrection, praise, and error correction"}, {"id": "9e0bf2f8-01bc-4ad6-9837-3ffc87cf09d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensory, communication, academic, and environmental fit"}], "description": "Students build predictable, culturally responsive environments."}, {"id": "f863f83e-bced-45d1-bf4f-c5d82201dca0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Functional assessment", "children": [{"id": "f8b51ce5-fa55-49d6-8ff5-3ecd0bc0e015", "type": "concept", "title": "Operational definitions and ABC data"}, {"id": "5e2523bb-9cf5-40e0-bd49-6fe51108c470", "type": "concept", "title": "Antecedent, consequence, setting event, and function hypotheses"}, {"id": "760b711a-f1d6-4042-ac67-1a8bc45fc641", "type": "concept", "title": "Indirect, descriptive, and experimental concepts"}], "description": "The goal is understanding what maintains behavior."}, {"id": "3fcd610f-abbf-4efa-ab6d-d0640abc0722", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Behavior intervention plans", "children": [{"id": "39d493e6-c9e3-4e3d-8554-9252c51b0780", "type": "concept", "title": "Prevention, replacement skills, reinforcement, and response strategies"}, {"id": "34fb8767-1894-43e5-bba7-481af1fe0638", "type": "concept", "title": "Data, fidelity, generalization, and crisis considerations"}, {"id": "2803e918-626a-4ea3-ae9b-5c74f9deeebf", "type": "concept", "title": "Family/student participation and dignity"}], "description": "Students teach alternatives and redesign contexts."}]}, {"id": "360874f8-343a-4f1f-bc2c-767f01be9a4b", "type": "topic", "title": "14. Social, Emotional, Mental Health, and Trauma-Informed Supports", "description": "Support regulation, relationships, safety, and mental health without pathologizing distress or lowering expectations.", "children": [{"id": "f8f13010-3a5c-49ee-a897-fa71edf23c75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social-emotional support", "children": [{"id": "8430d0fa-1707-4a3b-a26d-429fb7814f19", "type": "concept", "title": "Emotion recognition, regulation, problem solving, and relationships"}, {"id": "c8ed69c6-9d96-4c06-9d25-be1afdbb7998", "type": "concept", "title": "Class meetings and belonging"}, {"id": "537acc21-5bea-4d3a-afb0-d35adf3c062b", "type": "concept", "title": "Culturally responsive SEL"}], "description": "Students explicitly teach and embed skills."}, {"id": "579e92e9-a949-439a-8c7f-1646efaaa58a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trauma-informed practice", "children": [{"id": "4d062fd7-394b-4192-bfc8-28c6123530e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal precautions and avoiding retraumatization"}, {"id": "eac09d9d-2f32-44cf-971b-dd843354e69b", "type": "concept", "title": "Triggers, co-regulation, and restorative response"}, {"id": "901f4a49-48e8-4666-9364-c8e259048eb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundaries and referral to qualified professionals"}], "description": "The point is safety, predictability, choice, collaboration, and empowerment."}, {"id": "830c4271-f621-4c2d-acd7-fdcdcd3f6ac4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "School mental health", "children": [{"id": "7e4971d8-309d-4eb1-a87b-e757329e502d", "type": "concept", "title": "Anxiety, depression, school avoidance, grief, and crisis signs"}, {"id": "637c249b-40bf-4fa6-946e-770eff75c7ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Interconnected school/community systems"}, {"id": "08da9cf2-4175-4f7e-bd43-e72644460188", "type": "concept", "title": "Suicide/self-harm and threat-assessment procedures—follow policy immediately"}], "description": "Students know classroom roles and escalation pathways."}]}, {"id": "3c2b6d0b-1e19-47f5-8348-c5dbb2c3e76d", "type": "topic", "title": "15. Assistive Technology, AAC, Sensory, and Communication Access", "description": "Select and implement tools and supports that increase communication, learning, mobility, independence, and participation.", "children": [{"id": "2a8c4a84-0840-4dd2-a300-d83c899dc4a1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AT consideration", "children": [{"id": "386b3f69-72b6-457c-8325-1bfd64842bc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-, mid-, and high-tech tools"}, {"id": "c183683f-0a0a-48e4-84aa-022528f7ac99", "type": "concept", "title": "Trial, feature matching, data, training, and follow-up"}, {"id": "6ec85206-3bd4-466a-8b66-8c3a5437fba5", "type": "concept", "title": "IEP consideration, documentation, and abandonment prevention"}], "description": "Students use a person–task–environment process."}, {"id": "1f0c8f0e-9a72-4b2d-ba8c-268fae12c193", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AAC and communication", "children": [{"id": "15dc19f4-ed55-44e9-93ba-beba1ba2a32e", "type": "concept", "title": "Unaided/aided and symbol/text/speech systems"}, {"id": "3761b52a-4e29-41e8-9cab-a9fe2228e7e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Communication partners, modeling, wait time, and access methods"}, {"id": "3627d954-1f57-4a0e-806d-4c310c79c807", "type": "concept", "title": "Presume competence; AAC does not prevent speech"}], "description": "The goal is reliable communication across the day."}, {"id": "5c699324-6f43-4904-8a2e-b6fa19a1552e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sensory and physical access", "children": [{"id": "b262264b-b831-4fb4-b9d8-2d54fa83837f", "type": "concept", "title": "Vision, hearing, sensory processing, motor, and mobility needs"}, {"id": "4eaeccfa-a8e9-4668-a8b6-3692cadfdcbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Seating, positioning, switches, tactile/visual supports, and environmental adaptation"}, {"id": "55d7bc00-65d7-45fa-a40e-555d6993f226", "type": "concept", "title": "Emergency and field-trip access"}], "description": "Students collaborate with specialists to remove barriers."}]}, {"id": "f6010c89-3da8-4d9e-8964-06b47b98291e", "type": "topic", "title": "16. Co-Teaching and Collaborative Instruction", "description": "Build shared ownership of all learners through purposeful co-planning, instruction, assessment, and reflection.", "children": [{"id": "90beb1c6-d143-46a5-b529-467a43dad69a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Co-teaching models", "children": [{"id": "c72cdad9-6a81-463a-8d47-865a1185b7ea", "type": "concept", "title": "One teach/observe, station, parallel, alternative, team, and one teach/assist"}, {"id": "00ce35e4-9f73-4f05-9193-3a0e5df0107e", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding permanent assistant roles"}, {"id": "71ef8cdf-a165-4779-b01e-18eeb58092e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Flexible grouping and expertise sharing"}], "description": "Students choose models based on learning purpose."}, {"id": "10dd55fd-b80d-4581-b175-a1e33f758858", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Co-planning", "children": [{"id": "436a9b9b-d4fb-4ae4-a8fb-f4b6fa170469", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards, IEP goals, barriers, roles, materials, groups, and assessment"}, {"id": "cd3f34f4-73c1-4dc3-a18a-dcf4269d2a6b", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning protocols and protected time"}, {"id": "29ab0987-9973-4a39-a2f9-26dc751915ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Communication and conflict norms"}], "description": "The point is alignment before class."}, {"id": "384df4e5-bb6d-4bd7-b2ee-1a6e6f70580d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Co-assessment and improvement", "children": [{"id": "3553f4f2-9855-4562-88ef-771295f2fb56", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared data and grading"}, {"id": "a1dbd92e-425f-4aec-b985-c9dcaad1f403", "type": "concept", "title": "Feedback and role equity"}, {"id": "e348afdc-7271-4f98-b9ac-85e7f236dc98", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle of plan–teach–review–adjust"}], "description": "Students examine learner outcomes and partnership functioning."}]}, {"id": "057c5a35-25a8-4239-ba81-0a7d78183ddc", "type": "topic", "title": "17. Paraprofessional Partnership and Adult Support", "description": "Direct and collaborate with paraprofessionals ethically while promoting student autonomy and peer membership.", "children": [{"id": "4558c08c-ae35-48a7-9c32-09b531a5436b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Roles and boundaries", "children": [{"id": "d5cb5765-263b-413c-8b86-9e0ede944029", "type": "concept", "title": "Delegation under policy and qualification"}, {"id": "c5436cb7-9aa4-462f-ae40-14dcc3f69ed8", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality and professional conduct"}, {"id": "d84f9caf-f310-4a15-8305-97cde6bf014e", "type": "concept", "title": "Health/safety procedures and specialized training"}], "description": "Students understand teacher responsibility for instruction and supervision."}, {"id": "2ec734bc-5a99-448f-a23e-e2e1657a99e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Communication and feedback", "children": [{"id": "16c3fee8-3467-4c07-8081-a55fd070d637", "type": "concept", "title": "Plans, schedules, prompts, data, and debriefs"}, {"id": "4aac75ac-829e-410e-bed1-27c8b096cece", "type": "concept", "title": "Modeling, observation, coaching, and corrective feedback"}, {"id": "0c339927-1cb2-4955-9b0f-716eff1f80a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural/linguistic assets and team inclusion"}], "description": "The goal is clear, respectful partnership."}, {"id": "bee11ed2-fdce-4e89-bacd-9dbe012f4a7c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Independence and inclusion", "children": [{"id": "9ffaf232-ad2a-4c48-8870-9600112ebb66", "type": "concept", "title": "Prompt hierarchy and fading"}, {"id": "f7c761a4-f837-4b4a-b32e-30ea9daaffc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer supports and natural cues"}, {"id": "ed3ca70f-f59a-4a82-b561-8406b25edd12", "type": "concept", "title": "Data on independence, participation, and proximity"}], "description": "Students prevent overprompting and adult-created isolation."}]}, {"id": "1afee145-ccfa-479f-84d6-930e89215a74", "type": "topic", "title": "18. Family, Student, and Interprofessional Collaboration", "description": "Partner with families and learners as experts and coordinate with specialists around shared goals.", "children": [{"id": "71507138-250a-4cad-9ded-ec1d59d3c696", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Family partnership", "children": [{"id": "91cf6b4c-0e0a-49eb-82c9-98233a1fc21f", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths, priorities, culture, language, and family routines"}, {"id": "b0338dfb-f498-4c3c-962f-e71bf393538f", "type": "concept", "title": "Flexible meetings, interpreters, and understandable documents"}, {"id": "cc223dea-4b85-41d8-8c46-0b63d105b7b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflict, repair, and procedural rights"}], "description": "Students build trust through reciprocity and accessible communication."}, {"id": "67016e66-0a79-4af9-b61b-bc40a7875cf8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Student voice and self-determination", "children": [{"id": "796ed837-308f-4428-9dff-1eceaedde68d", "type": "concept", "title": "Preferences, strengths, goals, choices, and self-advocacy"}, {"id": "1502ab25-9c68-4b6a-98e3-57791c7d13f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Student-led IEP elements"}, {"id": "a04a0564-d259-49c6-8dea-f5d81ef1f51b", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision making, problem solving, and dignity of risk"}], "description": "The point is meaningful participation at every age."}, {"id": "a9387dae-309f-464b-bd19-ecbc26403ddb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interprofessional teamwork", "children": [{"id": "d72d610e-d654-420b-9178-22dfb67a6d61", "type": "concept", "title": "Special educator, SLP, OT, PT, psychologist, counselor, nurse, behavior specialist"}, {"id": "5cd9c17a-99b4-499c-b450-79f7a192d995", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared goals, role clarity, consultation, and transdisciplinary strategies"}, {"id": "f20759de-0f57-4baa-b392-368983145ba1", "type": "concept", "title": "Care coordination and community agencies"}], "description": "Students integrate expertise without fragmenting the child."}]}, {"id": "58889a90-8564-43d2-9afc-7609772a9f86", "type": "topic", "title": "19. Transition Planning Across Grades and into Adult Life", "description": "Treat transition as a continuous process of building agency, skills, experiences, and coordinated supports.", "children": [{"id": "04960ad4-0768-4841-bb06-d30e5bebe495", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Early and grade-to-grade transition", "children": [{"id": "d8c971bf-d115-4b23-a829-39c105741160", "type": "concept", "title": "Records, routines, relationships, and environment"}, {"id": "f9cd118f-9a3c-4c6e-9e73-c92eb73d61fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Kindergarten/middle-school transitions"}, {"id": "0baab6b0-f55c-495b-8186-ad00594eb202", "type": "concept", "title": "Summer, hospitalization, and reentry"}], "description": "Students plan continuity across classrooms, schools, and developmental changes."}, {"id": "b69bc380-0152-4b55-8cb5-68ac5d9340b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Secondary transition concepts", "children": [{"id": "09d674fe-9491-47f6-91ef-710aab91823c", "type": "concept", "title": "Education/training, employment, independent/community living"}, {"id": "57006149-bd50-44ac-9f6d-0bb23a04e6a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Age-appropriate transition assessment"}, {"id": "564ba96f-37db-483e-b84d-00f7eff0f5aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Courses, experiences, services, and agency linkages"}], "description": "Elementary teachers learn the long arc toward adult outcomes."}, {"id": "acaba4e2-f574-41cd-8dc8-d46ead7bc955", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Self-determination", "children": [{"id": "63b3e1b9-337f-4a49-a7af-274fc3ee39a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Choice, goal setting, self-monitoring, and self-advocacy"}, {"id": "48ae4be6-8e05-4340-a1bb-72195e14f54c", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths-based future planning"}, {"id": "aa767c47-f043-4a5e-b400-a60c6a7b3e13", "type": "concept", "title": "Supported decision-making concepts"}], "description": "The goal is increasing student control and participation."}]}, {"id": "410e96ce-03d8-4fcd-8342-30676210aaa0", "type": "topic", "title": "20. Culturally Sustaining, Linguistically Responsive, and Equitable Inclusion", "description": "Design support that respects identity and avoids racialized, linguistic, disability, and disciplinary inequities.", "children": [{"id": "2169c2cf-bf02-44eb-b34a-9d731ebe8527", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Culture and language", "children": [{"id": "78391910-7d5e-4d90-b4b8-ad79da955acd", "type": "concept", "title": "Language acquisition and cross-linguistic assessment"}, {"id": "4bf3fca9-0604-414f-bea8-0edc6c73fd96", "type": "concept", "title": "Home language as asset"}, {"id": "4eb598de-4b1d-4e9f-a618-bdc32dee5221", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpreters and bilingual specialists"}], "description": "Students distinguish multilingual development from disability."}, {"id": "a504d4e1-3ccf-4d4b-82e4-9967107e13cf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Disproportionality", "children": [{"id": "745fc3a3-480b-4530-8a86-40c00655092b", "type": "concept", "title": "Implicit bias and subjective categories"}, {"id": "cfc5b54f-8957-4dc6-ab3f-5954cb5ac881", "type": "concept", "title": "Opportunity to learn and instruction quality"}, {"id": "ca36612f-7570-462f-91dc-9ffa11e6b395", "type": "concept", "title": "Intersection of race, disability, gender, class, and language"}], "description": "The point is examining referral, identification, placement, discipline, and access patterns."}, {"id": "1e2725f1-3a92-4c43-9d14-5f6ba6a177e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Culturally sustaining practice", "children": [{"id": "32fc1e97-10e0-46fb-8cd2-8dd7473b8d35", "type": "concept", "title": "Identity-affirming texts and examples"}, {"id": "65bd52e7-7307-4855-accb-579137efbe22", "type": "concept", "title": "Community knowledge and funds of knowledge"}, {"id": "a79b0ecd-ab3a-4155-822b-f2c47f917648", "type": "concept", "title": "Restorative and non-exclusionary approaches"}], "description": "Students connect curriculum and support to learners’ communities."}]}, {"id": "616e2f2f-ed61-4d3b-a212-00221b092bf2", "type": "topic", "title": "21. Safety, Crisis Response, Restraint/Seclusion, and Ethical Safeguards", "description": "Prevent crises through proactive support and follow law and policy during safety emergencies.", "children": [{"id": "e3642fbf-bd53-4050-8c5c-9b20b7466a42", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prevention and de-escalation", "children": [{"id": "c3a42e99-e0c2-487f-a8fe-3198015fdff4", "type": "concept", "title": "Early warning signs and individualized plans"}, {"id": "0d7d6c05-80c2-4f20-8aa8-65e474e8ba8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Reduce demands/barriers and offer choices/space"}, {"id": "8208fceb-b5b7-4453-be9c-0e471f760887", "type": "concept", "title": "Call trained support and protect peers"}], "description": "Students use relationship, environment, communication, and regulation supports."}, {"id": "05901478-d054-4384-b0bd-76c58cf7bea2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Emergency response", "children": [{"id": "2d5f550a-5608-4819-b330-9cb08895340b", "type": "concept", "title": "Immediate danger threshold and emergency procedures"}, {"id": "439b565b-ab7a-472a-881d-3cf8e0cb67f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Medical, behavioral, elopement, abuse/neglect, and crisis reporting"}, {"id": "354a7782-4b9a-4f5e-b33e-0a9b5598673a", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation, family notification, and debrief"}], "description": "The goal is least restrictive, trained, policy-compliant action."}, {"id": "aea97f78-8e6c-421e-897f-745db1d6ab3f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Restraint and seclusion safeguards", "children": [{"id": "5eedcda2-0cd7-4b6a-8b31-df88c34c43b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Never for punishment, convenience, or instructional compliance"}, {"id": "381fb853-dad1-4593-8fb4-012d2b1edf96", "type": "concept", "title": "Follow current law/district policy and trained procedures"}, {"id": "8da65436-5007-44b6-89dd-7b5a4ff924a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Review inequities, injuries, antecedents, and prevention plan"}], "description": "Students understand serious risk and prevention."}]}, {"id": "8e1df10b-97c9-4b16-8d1c-b09d35d1dfc4", "type": "topic", "title": "22. Inclusive Field-Based Practice and Professional Portfolio", "description": "Integrate planning, instruction, collaboration, assessment, and reflection in authentic elementary settings.", "children": [{"id": "a0c6bfb3-b0b2-47fe-9e17-e1f39cb3641a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive lesson cycle", "children": [{"id": "7e94d7db-78a5-4451-a6aa-4eb4971278a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards, learner variability, UDL, SDI, accommodations, and AT"}, {"id": "d44ab45a-63ba-4e30-8f6c-b68dbd9dffb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Co-teaching/paraprofessional roles"}, {"id": "3466b39e-7be5-479a-ac89-bf0ad10715f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Formative data and student voice"}], "description": "Students plan, teach, collect evidence, and revise."}, {"id": "18f6421c-9202-4d3f-9e7c-b06c44807cb0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case-based collaboration", "children": [{"id": "2623abea-b981-4344-beaa-76976e2b8a60", "type": "concept", "title": "De-identified learner profile"}, {"id": "1eed2052-6110-471f-b706-e9d8042c4e78", "type": "concept", "title": "Family/student priorities and multidisciplinary input"}, {"id": "20c55b6a-c1de-49e2-92cb-1563aa5e5a43", "type": "concept", "title": "Barrier analysis and support plan"}], "description": "The point is ethical team reasoning without exposing confidential information."}, {"id": "cba65c91-8fef-4d05-b34a-88ea9d5947e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional growth", "children": [{"id": "bdfb1f73-85af-48cb-881d-4da7775b2a9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Observation feedback and reflection"}, {"id": "dcd89508-7610-4311-a5d5-1e953d385e9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio artifacts linked to course/legal competencies"}, {"id": "c9d3cfcb-19da-441d-93ae-876130cdc276", "type": "concept", "title": "Action plan for inclusive classroom practice"}], "description": "Students document competence and next steps."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$seipjson$::jsonb,
